From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: blade3: raise TYPEC1 sink capability to 20V/3A

TYPEC1 is the board's DC input: its VBUS is the only path into the
VCC12V~20V_DCIN rail, through a 30V/4A MOSFET and a 24V/3A fuse, and the
power tree specifies 20V at 3A for it.

The connector describes 1A on every sink PDO, so tcpm settles on 20V/1A --
20W on a rail specified for 60W. Raise both sink PDOs to 3000mA and drop the
PPS APDO; leave op-sink-microwatt, power-role and data-role alone.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-mixtile-blade3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-mixtile-blade3.dts
@@ -790,9 +790,8 @@
 			faster-pd-negotiation;
 			op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
 			sink-pdos =
-				<PDO_FIXED(5000, 1000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)
-				PDO_VAR(5000, 20000, 1000)
-				PDO_PPS_APDO(5000, 20000, 1000)>;
+				<PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)
+				PDO_VAR(5000, 20000, 3000)>;
 			source-pdos =
 				<PDO_FIXED(5000, 1000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
 
